cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The span contract: an admission decision for AI training jobs that cross a data hall boundary"
abstract: >-
  A single object a job carries when it asks to run across more than one data
  hall, carrying the twenty-one facts a scheduler, a compiler and a circuit
  controller must agree on before it starts, plus an optional tenancy
  declaration; six decisions the contract can return; three conditions under
  which it refuses rather than guesses; four tenant predicates that are listed
  as unchecked, not failed, when tenancy is undeclared; and a reference
  validator that turns the first into the second and prints its reasons,
  including the checks it declined to make.
authors:
  - family-names: Nanyonga
    given-names: Margaret
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dimaggi-ai/span-contract"
keywords:
  - distributed training
  - admission control
  - data center interconnect
  - optical circuit switching
  - capacity planning
  - multi-tenancy
